window.DOCS["6adba0140a679827eb07b236"]={"id":"6adba0140a679827eb07b236","summary":{"title_zh":"議程項目 8(b) 主席非正式文本（第二版）：全球環境基金第九次增資期間的財務機制","what":"這是主席整理的非正式文本（第二版），供第一工作小組討論全球環境基金第九次增資期間的承諾與資源、基金的運作、資源分配，以及第十次增資期間資金需求的評估。大部分段落仍在方括號內，尚未定案。","points":["[敦促][請求]已開發國家締約方，並邀請自願承擔已開發國家義務的其他締約方與國家，為全球環境基金第九次增資期間作出捐款，以支持綱要的全面落實（動詞仍在括號中）。","請求全球環境基金加速提升其成效，包括強化各環境公約間的整合路徑、促進私部門資金，並減少交易成本、簡化取得程序與改善撥款的及時性。","歡迎全球環境基金在第九次增資期間的方針中納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，並以 20% 為願景目標、對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持以 35% 為願景基準。","請求全球生物多樣性綱要基金增加可預測、足夠且額外的資源，並請其與執行機構持續簡化與加速專案核准與撥款程序。","請求執行秘書為全球環境基金第七次四年一度審查的成效審查，以及基金存量審查，進行籌備工作。","請求執行秘書編寫報告，評估第十次增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）協助開發中國家締約方履行公約承諾所需的資金規模。"],"open":["第 1 至 3 段：第九次增補承諾總額（約 39 億美元，數字待 2026 年 10 月更新）的措辭（歡迎、承認或注意到並讚賞），以及是否以「深切關切」注意到較第八次減少 27% 的談判結果，或改稱整體資源仍不足以應付需求，尚無共識。","第 4 段：要求已開發國家締約方捐款的動詞是「敦促」還是「請求」，尚無共識。","第 11、12 段：全球環境基金治理的準則是否納入原住民族與地方社區、婦女與青年的參與；資源分配公式是否要避免因過去撥款率低而對某些國家不利（註 9）；以及原住民族與地方社區直接取得資金的條件（註 11、12），尚無共識。","第 25 段：是否為卡塔赫納議定書的生物安全專案預留特定資源，或僅是鼓勵開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交申請，尚無共識。","第 15、15bis、16、20 段：全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作與成效描述（括號內的措辭與數字），以及對處理時間與低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家的資料揭露要求，尚無共識。","第 34、36、39(a) 段與附件二、附件三：是否通過第十次增資期間資金需求完整評估的職權範圍、第七次四年一度審查的職權範圍，以及是否委託第七次四年一度審查報告，尚無共識。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p001.md","en":"Agenda item 8 (b)\nResource mobilization and financial\nmechanism: financial mechanism\nWorking Group I\n\nFinancial mechanism\nNon-paper\nThe Conference of the Parties,\nRecalling its decisions 15/15 of 19 December 2022 and 16/33 of 27 February 2025 pertaining\nto the assessment of funding needed by all eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least\ndeveloped countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition for\nthe implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity 1 and its Protocols for the ninth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2026–June 2030),\nRecalling also the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme\npriorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\nEnvironment Facility Trust Fund contained in annex I to decision 16/33,\nRecognizing that the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework2 is relevant to all\nbiodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements and the mandate\nof the Global Environment Facility,\n[1. [Welcomes][Acknowledges][Notes with appreciation] the pledges made as at 30 May\n2026 for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by participant\ncountries, namely, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, France,\nGermany, India, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Luxembourg, Mexico, Netherlands (Kingdom of the), New\nZealand, Norway, Slovenia, South Africa, Switzerland and Uzbekistan, which amounted to\napproximately 3.9 billion United States dollars, using the agreed reference exchange rates for the\nreplenishment period;3]\n[2. Notes with concern that the amount of 3.9 billion dollars is contributed by only 50 per\ncent of developed country Parties, and appreciates the contributions of developing country Parties,\nnamely, Brazil, China, Côte d’Ivoire, India, Mexico, South Africa and Uzbekistan;4]\n[3. [Notes with deep concern] that [the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the\nGlobal Environment Facility Trust Fund concluded with a reduction of 27 per cent compared with\nthe eighth replenishment period and that such a reduction comes at a time when Parties are expected\nto accelerate the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][the\noverall level of resources remains insufficient in the light of the scale of needs to implement the\nConvention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\nFramework, in particular Target 19 (a);]]5\n\n1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n2 Decision 15/4, annex.\n3 To be updated in October 2026.\n4 To be updated in October 2026.\n5 Operative paragraphs 1 to 3 were considered at the seventh meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation (see\n\nrecommendation 7/3). Recommendation 6/2, adopted at its sixth meeting, also contained a paragraph on the topic of the ninth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (para. 6), but that paragraph was not discussed at that\nmeeting. It is the understanding of the Secretariat that paragraphs 1 to 3 above reflect the discussions of the Subsidiary Body on\nthe subject and therefore supersede the not-negotiated paragraph 6 in recommendation 6/2. As a result, that paragraph has not\nbeen included in the present draft decision. For reference, it read as follows: “[Reiterates its appreciation to developed country\nParties, other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other donors that contributed\nactively to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\nin support of eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\n[the most environmentally vulnerable country Parties,] and Parties with economies in transition;]”.","blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 8 (b)\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 8 (b)<br />\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制<br />\n第一工作小組</p>"},{"md":"財務機制\n非正式文件（Non-paper）\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>財務機制<br />\n非正式文件（Non-paper）<br />\n締約方大會，</p>"},{"md":"**回顧**其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）為執行《生物多樣性公約》$^1$及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026年7月至2030年6月）所需資金之決議 15/15（2022年12月19日）及 16/33（2025年2月27日），","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）為執行《生物多樣性公約》<sup>1</sup>及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026年7月至2030年6月）所需資金之決議 15/15（2022年12月19日）及 16/33（2025年2月27日），</p>"},{"md":"**亦回顧**決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，本公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，本公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，</p>"},{"md":"**認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^2$》與所有生物多樣性相關公約、其他多邊環境協議以及全球環境基金之授權相關，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>2</sup>》與所有生物多樣性相關公約、其他多邊環境協議以及全球環境基金之授權相關，</p>"},{"md":"[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 參與國截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；$^3$]","html":"<p>[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 參與國截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；<sup>3</sup>]</p>"},{"md":"[2. **憂慮地注意到** 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並**歡迎**開發中國家締約方的貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；$^4$]","html":"<p>[2. <strong>憂慮地注意到</strong> 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並<strong>歡迎</strong>開發中國家締約方的貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；<sup>4</sup>]</p>"},{"md":"[3. [**深感憂慮地注意到**] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此類減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際] [鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍顯不足；]]$^5$","html":"<p>[3. [<strong>深感憂慮地注意到</strong>] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此類減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際] [鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍顯不足；]]<sup>5</sup></p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"$^1$ 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^2$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^3$ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n$^4$ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n$^5$ 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所採納的建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議上進行討論。秘書處理解，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代建議 6/2 中未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而積極貢獻於全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。","html":"<p><sup>1</sup> 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>2</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>3</sup> 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n<sup>4</sup> 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n<sup>5</sup> 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所採納的建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議上進行討論。秘書處理解，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代建議 6/2 中未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而積極貢獻於全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。</p>"}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p002.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n4.\n[Urges][Requests] developed country Parties, and invites other Parties that voluntarily\nassume the obligations of developed country Parties and other countries, to make contributions for\nthe ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of the full\nimplementation of the Framework and in accordance with the provisions of Article 20 of the\nConvention;\n5.\nWelcomes the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the\nseventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;6\n6.\nAlso welcomes the improved disaggregation of co-financing by source in the report of\nthe Council of the Global Environment Facility and encourages the Facility to continue to enhance\nthe transparency and granularity of future reporting on the various sources of co-financing;\n7.\nNotes with appreciation that the programming directions for the ninth replenishment\nperiod have been designed to deliver on all elements of the four-year outcome-oriented framework\nof biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment\nperiod adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its sixteenth meeting,7 reflecting the effective\nresponse to the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n8.\nWelcomes the allocation of 35 per cent of the ninth replenishment resources to the\nbiodiversity focal area, which is the largest focal area, and the aim of committing at least 70 per cent\nof funding to biodiversity over that period, according to the Rio marker methodology of the\nDevelopment Assistance Committee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and\nDevelopment;\n9.\nAlso welcomes the inclusion in the programming directions and policy\nrecommendations of the Global Environment Facility for the ninth replenishment period of the\nindigenous people and local community conservation initiative, 8 an aspirational target of\nprogramming 20 per cent of resources to support indigenous peoples and local communities and\nstrengthened support to least developed countries and small island developing States, with an\naspirational benchmark of 35 per cent for those countries, as well as the introduction of the\naspirational target of programming 25 per cent to mobilize private capital;\n10. Further welcomes the establishment of the Ad Hoc Governance Working Group of the\nCouncil of the Global Environment Facility under the ninth replenishment of the Facility, in response\nto decision 16/33;\n[11. Requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria\n[set out in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025] [and decision 17/--], ensuring a\ndemocratic and transparent system of governance that is fair, equitable, inclusive, efficient and\nrepresentative[, while facilitating the full and effective participation of indigenous people and local\ncommunities, women and youth];]\n12. Requests the Global Environment Facility to accelerate efforts to further strengthen its\neffectiveness, including by:\n(a) Improving integration pathways, approaches and integrated programmes that deliver\nsystem-wide environmental benefits to improve synergies among environmental conventions, while\nensuring that such programmes take into account their respective mandates, remain country-driven,\nresponsive to national circumstances and priorities, and implemented through meaningful\nengagement with national executing agencies from recipient countries;\n(b) Enabling and facilitating private sector financing aligned with the objectives of the\nConvention through its blended finance programme funding window and the provision of predictable\nsupport to eligible Parties, with a view to developing projects and programmes that enable greater\n6 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n7 Decision 16/33, annex I.\n8 Building on previous iterations of the Inclusive Conservation Initiative at an expanded level of 100 million dollars,\n\n2/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"4.\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方及其他國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增額提供貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面實施，並符合《公約》第 20 條之規定；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方及其他國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增額提供貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面實施，並符合《公約》第 20 條之規定；</p>"},{"md":"5.\n**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶</p>"},{"md":"6.\n亦**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源所進行之改良式分類，並**鼓勵**基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細粒度；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源所進行之改良式分類，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細粒度；</p>"},{"md":"7.\n**注意到**第九次增額期間之規劃方向，已旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議上所通過之《公約》及其議定書四年期成果導向生物多樣性優先事項框架的所有要素，⁷ 反映了對締約方所提供指引之有效回應，並對此表示讚賞；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>注意到</strong>第九次增額期間之規劃方向，已旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議上所通過之《公約》及其議定書四年期成果導向生物多樣性優先事項框架的所有要素，⁷ 反映了對締約方所提供指引之有效回應，並對此表示讚賞；</p>"},{"md":"8.\n**歡迎**將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；</p>"},{"md":"9.\n亦**歡迎**在全球環境基金第九次增額期間之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸ 即一項旨在投入 20% 資源以支持原住民族與地方社區之願景目標，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家之支持（對該等國家之願景基準為 35%），以及引入旨在動員私人資本之 25% 投入願景目標；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>在全球環境基金第九次增額期間之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸ 即一項旨在投入 20% 資源以支持原住民族與地方社區之願景目標，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家之支持（對該等國家之願景基準為 35%），以及引入旨在動員私人資本之 25% 投入願景目標；</p>"},{"md":"10. 進一步**歡迎**為因應決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特別治理工作小組；","html":"<p>10. 進一步<strong>歡迎</strong>為因應決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特別治理工作小組；</p>"},{"md":"[11. **請求**全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、具包容性、高效且具代表性的民主且透明之治理系統，[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之全面且有效參與]；]","html":"<p>[11. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、具包容性、高效且具代表性的民主且透明之治理系統，[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之全面且有效參與]；]</p>"},{"md":"12. **請求**全球環境基金加速其進一步強化成效之努力，包括透過以下方式：\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間之綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家主導，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資金窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使與《公約》目標一致之私營部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能實現更大規模之專案與計畫；","html":"<p>12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金加速其進一步強化成效之努力，包括透過以下方式：<br />\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間之綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家主導，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；<br />\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資金窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使與《公約》目標一致之私營部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能實現更大規模之專案與計畫；</p>"},{"md":"***\n⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元之包容性保育倡議基礎上，","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。<br />\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。<br />\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元之包容性保育倡議基礎上，</p>"}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p003.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\nprivate sector investment and financial flows, including through long-term enabling policy\nframeworks, incentives, regulations, blended finance tools and the development of financially viable,\ninvestment-ready biodiversity finance projects and pipelines, while recognizing that such\ninvestments complement public finance;\n(c) Promoting whole-of-society and whole-of-government approaches, as appropriate and\nin accordance with national circumstances, to strengthen programme and project ownership at the\nnational level and the alignment of biodiversity actions with nationally identified priorities, national\nbiodiversity strategies and action plans, national development priorities, and policy coherence;\n(d) Continuing to improve its system of resource allocation[9] [[, including by continuing\nto maximize the generation of global environmental benefits and recognizing the role of indigenous\npeoples and local communities in achieving them, and to improve the allocation performance of its\nimplementing entities] [by enhancing transparency, equity, predictability and responsiveness to the\n[relevant][specific] needs and priorities of developing country Parties, including small island\ndeveloping States and least developed countries]];\n(e) Sustaining enhanced support for all eligible Parties, in particular least developed\ncountries, small island developing States [and the most environmentally vulnerable countries], by\nreducing transaction costs, simplifying access procedures across existing Global Environment\nFacility focal areas and financing windows[, including through direct access modalities via national\nimplementing agencies,] and improving the timeliness and predictability of financial support,\nmeasured by the date of first disbursement to the recipient country;\n(f)\nDeepening accessible support for indigenous peoples and local communities, in line\nwith element 8 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention\nrelated to indigenous peoples and local communities to 203010 (access, including direct access, to\nfunding for indigenous peoples and local communities for the conservation, restoration and\nsustainable use of biodiversity), including by developing guidance on the 20 per cent portfolio-wide\ntarget for indigenous peoples and local communities, which includes the [dedicated][[direct]\naccess][11] modalities;\n[(g) Strengthening the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive\nparticipation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth[, including in decisionmaking,] in accordance with the national legislation of concerned Parties;]\n(h) Continuing to promote country-driven national initiatives and regionally coordinated\nregional and multi-country initiatives[, including transboundary initiatives, with effective\nparticipation [and formal approval] [of national focal points for the Convention and relevant national\nauthorities] [and formal approval of operational focal points for the Global Environment Facility]];\n(i)\nEnsuring that Global Environment Facility support for the implementation of the\nConvention[, including support [through direct access [ 12 ]] for the implementation, monitoring,\nupdate and review of national biodiversity strategies and action plans,] is country-led and aligned\nwith [national biodiversity strategies and action plans and] the targets of the Framework;\n\n[9 Ensuring that any performance-based element of the allocation formula, including any measure of past disbursement, does not\ndisadvantage Parties the disbursement rates of which reflect the capacity constraints that the financial mechanism exists to\nrelieve, consistent with paragraph 4 of Article 20 of the Convention.]\n10 Decision 16/4, annex.\n[11 Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to established\nGlobal Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global Environment Facility,\nwhich is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n12 [Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to\nestablished Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n\n3/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"私營部門投資與金融流動，包括透過長期賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合型金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具備投資條件之生物多樣性金融專案與案源管道，同時承認此類投資與公共財政相輔相成；\n(c) 在適當情況下並根據國家國情，促進全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級的計畫與專案所有權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家認定的優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性保持一致；\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益的產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在實現這些效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增強透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]];\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序[, 包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支持的及時性與可預測性（以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準），以持續為所有符合資格之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供強化支持；\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支持，以符合《公約》第八條第 (j) 項工作計畫之第八要素，以及《公約》其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年¹⁰（包括對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過制定關於原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標之指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性之參與[, 包括在決策過程中的參與;];]\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，且須有效參與 [與正式核准] [《公約》國家焦點與相關國家主管機關] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]];\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行《公約》之支持[, 包括支持[透過直接取得 [12] ]以執行、監測、更新與審查國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]《綱要》之目標保持一致；","html":"<p>私營部門投資與金融流動，包括透過長期賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合型金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具備投資條件之生物多樣性金融專案與案源管道，同時承認此類投資與公共財政相輔相成；<br />\n(c) 在適當情況下並根據國家國情，促進全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級的計畫與專案所有權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家認定的優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性保持一致；<br />\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益的產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在實現這些效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增強透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]];<br />\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序[, 包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支持的及時性與可預測性（以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準），以持續為所有符合資格之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供強化支持；<br />\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支持，以符合《公約》第八條第 (j) 項工作計畫之第八要素，以及《公約》其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年¹⁰（包括對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過制定關於原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標之指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；<br />\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性之參與[, 包括在決策過程中的參與;];]<br />\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，且須有效參與 [與正式核准] [《公約》國家焦點與相關國家主管機關] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]];<br />\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行《公約》之支持[, 包括支持[透過直接取得 [12] ]以執行、監測、更新與審查國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]《綱要》之目標保持一致；</p>"},{"md":"[9 確保分配公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款率之衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出因能力限制而需透過財務機制予以緩解之締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]\n¹⁰ 決議 16/4，附件。\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在獲得全球環境基金執行焦點之核准後進行，該核准應與《公約》國家焦點協調進行。]\n¹² [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在獲得全球環境基金執行焦點之核准後進行，該核准應與《公約》國家焦點協調進行。]","html":"<p>[9 確保分配公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款率之衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出因能力限制而需透過財務機制予以緩解之締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]<br />\n¹⁰ 決議 16/4，附件。<br />\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在獲得全球環境基金執行焦點之核准後進行，該核准應與《公約》國家焦點協調進行。]<br />\n¹² [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在獲得全球環境基金執行焦點之核准後進行，該核准應與《公約》國家焦點協調進行。]</p>"}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p004.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n(j)\nContinuing to support the development and implementation of national biodiversity\nfinance plans or similar instruments and their integration, where applicable, into national policies\nand priorities;\n(k) Continuing to advance collaboration, coherence and complementarity across\nmultilateral climate funds and other sources of finance relevant to the implementation of the\nFramework;\n(l)\nStrengthening national institutional and technical capacities for project preparation,\nimplementation, monitoring and reporting;\n[(m) Simplifying project development guidance;]\n(n) Reporting on the attainment of the targets mentioned in paragraph 9 above and on\ndisaggregated data on programming, approvals and disbursement by recipient country or region;\n[(o) Improving the transparency and granularity of reporting on biodiversity-related finance,\nincluding by distinguishing between financing for which biodiversity is a principal objective and\nfinancing for which it is a significant objective under the Rio marker methodology, taking into\naccount the qualitative nature of the Rio markers and by clarifying the extent to which such financing\ncontribute to the implementation of the Framework;]\n13. Also requests the Global Environment Facility to report to the Conference of the Parties\nat its eighteenth meeting on the resources of the biodiversity focal area for the ninth replenishment\nperiod of its Trust Fund expressed in United States dollars at the final replenishment level, together\nwith the corresponding figure for the eighth replenishment period, and on the share of resources\noriginally programmed and subsequently disbursed to small island developing States, presented\nseparately from least developed countries;\n14. Recognizes the value of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in complementing the\nGlobal Environment Facility Trust Fund by providing financial support to eligible developing\ncountry Parties for achieving the goals and targets of the Framework;\n[15. [Takes note [with appreciation] of] [Welcomes][Reiterates its expression of\nappreciation for] the operationalization of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund [within X time]\n[[in record time] with a [one step approval process] [streamlined project cycle[, the demonstration of\nspeed of [approval [of projects]][delivery]]]] and the achievement to date of the three portfolio targets\n[pertaining to [including on] least developed countries and small islands developing States,\nindigenous peoples and local communities[, women and youth,] [and resources programmed through\ninternational financial institutions]];]\n[15bis. [Welcomes] [Reiterates its expression of appreciation for] the operationalization of the\nGlobal Biodiversity Framework Fund with a [one step approval process] [streamlined project cycle,\nthe demonstration of speed of approval of projects] and the achievement to date of the [three]\nportfolio targets;]\n[16. [Takes note with] [Expresses its] [deep concern] of the information on the Global\nBiodiversity Framework Fund contained in the report of the Council of the Global Environment\nFacility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, [in particular the limited scale\nof capitalization to date in relation to [supporting] the financing needs for the implementation of the\nKunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][ and [invites the Fund to support eligible\nParties and accessing the Fund in particular those that have not yet received support][ that many\neligible Parties have not yet received support from the Fund]];]\n17. Reiterates the call made by the Council of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund at\nits sixth meeting for new and additional contributions from all sources to support the continuous,\nrapid and robust capitalization of the Fund [, without affecting existing obligations and mandates][,\nwithout prejudice to the obligations of developed country Parties under Article 20 of the Convention\n4/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"(j)\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與執行，以及在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；\n(k)\n持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與執行綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；\n(l)\n強化國家在專案準備、執行、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；\n[(m) 簡化專案開發指南；]\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國或區域分類之計畫編列、核准與撥款的分解資料；\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，並澄清此類融資對執行綱要的貢獻程度；]","html":"<p>(j)<br />\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與執行，以及在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；<br />\n(k)<br />\n持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與執行綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；<br />\n(l)<br />\n強化國家在專案準備、執行、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；<br />\n[(m) 簡化專案開發指南；]<br />\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國或區域分類之計畫編列、核准與撥款的分解資料；<br />\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，並澄清此類融資對執行綱要的貢獻程度；]</p>"},{"md":"13. 亦請求全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，報告其信託基金第九期增資期間，以美元表示的生物多樣性重點領域資源之最終增補水平，並附上第八期增資期間的對應數字，以及原先計畫編列並隨後撥款予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且此項報告應與低度開發國家分開呈現；","html":"<p>13. 亦請求全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，報告其信託基金第九期增資期間，以美元表示的生物多樣性重點領域資源之最終增補水平，並附上第八期增資期間的對應數字，以及原先計畫編列並隨後撥款予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且此項報告應與低度開發國家分開呈現；</p>"},{"md":"14. 認可全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；","html":"<p>14. 認可全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；</p>"},{"md":"[15. [注意到 [並表示讚賞] ] [歡迎][重申對……表示讚賞] 全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作 [在 X 時間內] [[創紀錄的速度] 以 [一步核准程序] [精簡的專案週期[, 展現了 [核准 [專案] 的] [效率]]]] 且迄今已達成三項投資組合目標 [涉及 [包括對] 低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、原住民族與地方社區[, 女性與青年,] [以及透過國際金融機構計畫編列的資源]]；]","html":"<p>[15. [注意到 [並表示讚賞] ] [歡迎][重申對……表示讚賞] 全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作 [在 X 時間內] [[創紀錄的速度] 以 [一步核准程序] [精簡的專案週期[, 展現了 [核准 [專案] 的] [效率]]]] 且迄今已達成三項投資組合目標 [涉及 [包括對] 低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、原住民族與地方社區[, 女性與青年,] [以及透過國際金融機構計畫編列的資源]]；]</p>"},{"md":"[15bis. [歡迎] [重申對……表示讚賞] 全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作，具備 [一步核准程序] [精簡的專案週期，展現了專案核准的速度] 且迄今已達成 [三項] 投資組合目標；]","html":"<p>[15bis. [歡迎] [重申對……表示讚賞] 全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作，具備 [一步核准程序] [精簡的專案週期，展現了專案核准的速度] 且迄今已達成 [三項] 投資組合目標；]</p>"},{"md":"[16. [注意到] [表示其] [深切關注] 全球環境基金理事會在第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含的關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊，[特別是迄今資本化規模有限，相對於 [支持] 執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的融資需求][ 且 [邀請基金支持符合條件的締約方並使用該基金，特別是那些尚未獲得支持的締約方][ 許多符合條件的締約方尚未從基金獲得支持]]；]","html":"<p>[16. [注意到] [表示其] [深切關注] 全球環境基金理事會在第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含的關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊，[特別是迄今資本化規模有限，相對於 [支持] 執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的融資需求][ 且 [邀請基金支持符合條件的締約方並使用該基金，特別是那些尚未獲得支持的締約方][ 許多符合條件的締約方尚未從基金獲得支持]]；]</p>"},{"md":"17. 重申全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在其第六次會議上提出的呼籲，要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，[, 在不影響現有義務與職責的情況下][, 在不損害公約第二十條規定之已開發國家締約方義務的前提下","html":"<p>17. 重申全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在其第六次會議上提出的呼籲，要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，[, 在不影響現有義務與職責的情況下][, 在不損害公約第二十條規定之已開發國家締約方義務的前提下</p>"}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p005.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\nand with a view to attracting contributions from sovereign, non-sovereign, private sector,\nphilanthropic and financial actors];\n18. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund to enhance efforts to mobilize\npredictable, adequate and additional resources from all sources and report on the implementation of\nits resource mobilization strategy for the period from July 2026 to June 2030, including through\ndisaggregated information on pledges and paid contributions by sources of finance;\n19. Invites developed country Parties and Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of\ndeveloped country Parties, other governments at all levels, the private sector and philanthropic\norganizations to make or increase their contributions to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;\n20. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and its implementing agencies to\ncontinue to enhance its efforts to:\n(a) Facilitate, as appropriate, the mobilization of financial resources from all sources,\nrecognizing the need for further capitalization;\n(b) Improve co-financing arrangements as appropriate, whilst recognizing that co-financing is\nnot a requirement, and without creating additional barriers to access or shifting the financial burden\nto all eligible countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\nalso taking into consideration the specific needs of vulnerable countries, in the context of paragraph\n6 and 7 of article 20;\n(c) Simplify and expedite, where appropriate and taking into account country ownership,\nproject approval and disbursement procedures, including the endorsement process and disbursement\nprocesses for approved projects under the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund [through transparent,\npredictable and timebound procedures];\n[(d)\n\nSimplify implementation procedures[, where appropriate];]\n\n[(e)\n\nReduce project cycle processing times;]\n\n[(f) Report on processing and disbursement times disaggregated for least developed\ncountries and small island developing States;]\n[(g) Provide necessary resources, fully disbursed allocated funds and complete\norganizational work, including at the national level, in support of the preparation of the eighth\nnational reports by the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]\n[(h) Enhance equitable access, including by considering measures to facilitate access for\neligible country Parties that have not yet received support from the Global Biodiversity Framework\nFund;]]\n21. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive Secretary\nof the Convention[, to consider supporting,][to provide support to] [all] eligible Parties in line with\nits mandate, for:\n(a) [National platforms or ]existing national coordination mechanisms designed to aid\nproject preparation, as necessary[, and track ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities;]\n[(b) Capacity-building and readiness support for national implementing agencies, including\nfor accreditation;]\n(c) The preparation and submission of national reports on the implementation of the\nConvention, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety13 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic\nResources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, taking into\naccount national circumstances;14\n13 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n14 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619.\n\n5/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"以及為了吸引來自主權、非主權、私營部門、慈善與金融參與者之貢獻]；","html":"<p>以及為了吸引來自主權、非主權、私營部門、慈善與金融參與者之貢獻]；</p>"},{"md":"18. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略之執行情況，包括透過按財務來源分類之承諾與已支付貢獻之細分資訊；","html":"<p>18. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略之執行情況，包括透過按財務來源分類之承諾與已支付貢獻之細分資訊；</p>"},{"md":"19. **邀請**已開發國家締約方以及自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；","html":"<p>19. <strong>邀請</strong>已開發國家締約方以及自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；</p>"},{"md":"20. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：","html":"<p>20. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 在適當情況下，促進從所有來源動員財務資源，並承認進一步增資之必要性；","html":"<p>(a) 在適當情況下，促進從所有來源動員財務資源，並承認進一步增資之必要性；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 在適當情況下改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成額外的取得障礙，或將財務負擔轉移至所有符合資格之國家，特別是最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並同時考慮第 20 條第 6 段與第 7 段背景下脆弱國家之特定需求；","html":"<p>(b) 在適當情況下改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成額外的取得障礙，或將財務負擔轉移至所有符合資格之國家，特別是最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並同時考慮第 20 條第 6 段與第 7 段背景下脆弱國家之特定需求；</p>"},{"md":"(c) 在適當情況下並考量國家自主權，簡化並加速專案核准與撥款程序，包括全球生物多樣性綱要基金下已核准專案之認可程序與撥款程序 [透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序]；","html":"<p>(c) 在適當情況下並考量國家自主權，簡化並加速專案核准與撥款程序，包括全球生物多樣性綱要基金下已核准專案之認可程序與撥款程序 [透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序]；</p>"},{"md":"[(d)\n簡化執行程序[, 在適當情況下];]","html":"<p>[(d)<br />\n簡化執行程序[, 在適當情況下];]</p>"},{"md":"[(e)\n縮短專案週期之處理時間；]","html":"<p>[(e)<br />\n縮短專案週期之處理時間；]</p>"},{"md":"[(f) 針對最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，報告按類別細分之處理與撥款時間；]","html":"<p>[(f) 針對最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，報告按類別細分之處理與撥款時間；]</p>"},{"md":"[(g) 提供必要資源、全額撥付已分配資金並完成組織工作，包括在國家層級，以支持在第十八次締約方大會前完成第八次國家報告之準備工作；]","html":"<p>[(g) 提供必要資源、全額撥付已分配資金並完成組織工作，包括在國家層級，以支持在第十八次締約方大會前完成第八次國家報告之準備工作；]</p>"},{"md":"[(h) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之符合資格締約方之取得；]]","html":"<p>[(h) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之符合資格締約方之取得；]]</p>"},{"md":"21. **請求**全球環境基金與公約執行秘書合作[, 考慮支持，][提供支持予] [所有] 符合資格之締約方，並符合其職權範圍，以用於：","html":"<p>21. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與公約執行秘書合作[, 考慮支持，][提供支持予] [所有] 符合資格之締約方，並符合其職權範圍，以用於：</p>"},{"md":"(a) [國家平台或] 現有的國家協調機制，旨在必要時協助專案準備[, 並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項；]","html":"<p>(a) [國家平台或] 現有的國家協調機制，旨在必要時協助專案準備[, 並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項；]</p>"},{"md":"[(b) 為國家執行機構提供能力建構與準備支持，包括用於認證之支持；]","html":"<p>[(b) 為國家執行機構提供能力建構與準備支持，包括用於認證之支持；]</p>"},{"md":"(c) 在考量國家情況下，準備並提交關於執行公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書¹³ 以及關於遺傳資源取得及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享之名古屋議定書之國家報告；¹⁴","html":"<p>(c) 在考量國家情況下，準備並提交關於執行公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書¹³ 以及關於遺傳資源取得及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享之名古屋議定書之國家報告；¹⁴</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"¹³ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹⁴ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30 619 號。","html":"<p>¹³ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹⁴ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30 619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p006.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n(d) Capacity-building for leveraging private sector financing, including from capital\nmarkets, through, inter alia, innovative mechanisms and blended finance, and for developing\nfinancially viable projects, with robust safeguards[ to avoid increasing debt vulnerabilities];\n22. Requests the Executive Secretary to undertake preparatory work for the stocktake\nreview of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund referred to in paragraph 29 of decision 15/15,[\nin accordance with annex III to the present decision], in conjunction with its seventh quadrennial\nreview of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, [recognizing that the stocktake shall inform,\nbut not prejudge, consideration by the Conference of the Parties of the future institutional structure\nof the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention];\n[23. Invites the Global Environment Facility to facilitate financial support for eligible Parties\nthat have not yet received support for the development of the national biodiversity strategies and\naction plans and national targets or the preparation of national reports;]\n[24. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in consultation with recipient countries and\nthe Executive Secretary, to review the effectiveness of projects funded during its seventh and eighth\ncycles for the development of national biodiversity strategies and actions plans and national reports\n[under the Convention and its Protocols] and to report on the measures that it has taken to address\nidentified challenges [for][to adjust accordingly] the preparation of the eight national report [to the\nSubsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before][at] the eighteenth meeting of the\nConference of the Parties;]\n25. [Requests that specific resources be reserved for][Encourages developing country\nParties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety to submit to the Global Environment Facility]\nbiosafety projects under the Protocol, given the small number of such projects funded in previous\nrounds;\n26. Requests the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Secretariat of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, to prepare a draft four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity\nprogramme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols related to the use of Facility resources for\nbiodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034, taking into consideration the global review\nof collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, [and addressing expressly the access\nmodalities and capacity constraints of developing countries Parties, in particular least developed\ncountries and small island developing States, consistent with paragraphs 5 and 6 of Article 20 of the\nConvention,] for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before\nthe eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and subsequent adoption by the Conference\nof the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n[27. Emphasizes that the preparation of the four-year outcome-oriented framework of\nbiodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the tenth replenishment\nperiod of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund is without prejudice to the process established\nin decision 16/34 regarding the institutional structure for the financial mechanism provided under\nArticle 21 of the Convention.]\n28. Adopts the additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility contained in annex I\nto the present decision, and requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to include\ninformation regarding the implementation of the additional guidance in its reports to the Conference\nof the Parties;\n29. Notes the information on funding needs received from 45 eligible Parties and the\ncompilation and analysis of that information transmitted by the Secretariat of the Convention on\nBiological Diversity to the Global Environment Facility to help with the negotiations for the ninth\nreplenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n\n6/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"(d) 透過創新機制與混合金融等方式，強化利用來自資本市場等私部門融資之能力建構，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施 [以避免增加債務脆弱性] 之專案；","html":"<p>(d) 透過創新機制與混合金融等方式，強化利用來自資本市場等私部門融資之能力建構，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施 [以避免增加債務脆弱性] 之專案；</p>"},{"md":"22. **請求**執行秘書針對決議 15/15 第 29 段所提及之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核之準備工作，[依據本決議附件 III]，並與其第七次財務機制有效性四年一度審查一併進行，[並承認清查應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；","html":"<p>22. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書針對決議 15/15 第 29 段所提及之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核之準備工作，[依據本決議附件 III]，並與其第七次財務機制有效性四年一度審查一併進行，[並承認清查應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；</p>"},{"md":"[23. **邀請**全球環境基金為尚未獲得制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標或編製國家報告支援之合資格締約方，提供財務支援之便利；]","html":"<p>[23. <strong>邀請</strong>全球環境基金為尚未獲得制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標或編製國家報告支援之合資格締約方，提供財務支援之便利；]</p>"},{"md":"[24. **請求**全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為開發 [依據《公約》及其議定書] 之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為因應已識別之挑戰 [針對][以相應調整] 第八份國家報告之編製所採取之措施，[向執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議提交][於第十八次締約方大會提交]；]","html":"<p>[24. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為開發 [依據《公約》及其議定書] 之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為因應已識別之挑戰 [針對][以相應調整] 第八份國家報告之編製所採取之措施，[向執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議提交][於第十八次締約方大會提交]；]</p>"},{"md":"25. [**請求保留特定資源用於**][**鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交] 議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；","html":"<p>25. [<strong>請求保留特定資源用於</strong>][**鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交] 議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；</p>"},{"md":"26. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量全球對於實施綱要集體進展之審查，[並明確處理開發中國家締約方（特別是最低開發國與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，且與《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段一致，] 為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，針對《公約》及其議定書下與利用基金資源於生物多樣性相關之生物多樣性計畫優先事項，準備一份以成果為導向之四年期框架草案，供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議予以採納；","html":"<p>26. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量全球對於實施綱要集體進展之審查，[並明確處理開發中國家締約方（特別是最低開發國與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，且與《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段一致，] 為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，針對《公約》及其議定書下與利用基金資源於生物多樣性相關之生物多樣性計畫優先事項，準備一份以成果為導向之四年期框架草案，供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議予以採納；</p>"},{"md":"[27. **強調**為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書下之四年期成果導向生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]","html":"<p>[27. <strong>強調</strong>為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書下之四年期成果導向生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]</p>"},{"md":"28. **採納**本決議附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並**請求**全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關執行該附加指南之資訊；","html":"<p>28. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關執行該附加指南之資訊；</p>"},{"md":"29. **注意到**從 45 個合資格締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資之談判；","html":"<p>29. <strong>注意到</strong>從 45 個合資格締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資之談判；</p>"}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p007.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n30. Takes note of the report on the assessment of the amount of funds needed for the\nimplementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\nEnvironment Facility Trust Fund;15\n31. Notes the limited number of submissions from eligible Parties and therefore limited\ninformation available for assessing the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the\nConvention and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework for the\nninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n[32. Also notes the importance of a realistic assessment of funding necessary and available\nfor the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Framework for the ninth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility;]\n[33. Emphasizes the need to strengthen technical and institutional support for eligible Parties,\nso that their needs are fully reflected in future assessments;]\n[34. Adopts the terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are\nnecessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small\nisland developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\nprovided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for\nthe tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June\n2034), as contained in annex II to the present decision, noting that the assessment should be\nconducted in a manner that avoids disproportionate administrative burdens and provides for financial\nand technical support for data collection in developing country Parties;]\n[35. Encourages Parties to establish national platforms for planning and monitoring\nbiodiversity projects that and are accessible to stakeholders and regularly updated;]\n[36. Adopts the terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of\nthe financial mechanism, as contained in annex III to the present decision;]\n37. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations, as well as indigenous\npeoples and local communities, women and youth, to contribute to and participate in the seventh\nquadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as outlined in the terms of\nreference;\n38. Emphasizes the importance of integrating [in the quadrennial review] specific indicators\nfor eligible Parties, in particular on the number of projects funded, disbursement times and impact\non local communities;\n39.\n\nRequests the Executive Secretary[, subject to availability of resources]:\n\n[(a) To commission and make available a report on the seventh quadrennial review of the\neffectiveness of the financial mechanism in time for consideration by the Conference of the Parties\nat its eighteenth meeting;]\n(b) To prepare a report on the full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\nassist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\ndeveloping States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\nprovided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for\nthe tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, for consideration by\nthe Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the\nConference of the Parties and by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n[(c) To further strengthen collaboration and engagement with financial institutions and\nstakeholders, especially those recognized by the Global Environment Facility, the Green Climate\nFund and the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development, in order to accelerate the\n15 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.\n\n7/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"30. **注意到**關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所需資金規模評估之報告；15\n31. **注意到**符合資格之締約方提交之報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所需用於履行《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之資金規模，可用資訊有限；\n[32. **亦注意到**針對全球環境基金第九期增資，對履行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需之必要且可用資金進行務實評估的重要性；]\n[33. **強調**有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映於未來的評估中；]\n[34. **採納**本決議附件 II 所載之職權範圍，旨在針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），根據締約方所提供之指引，針對協助開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下承諾所需之資金規模進行全面評估；並注意到該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]\n[35. **鼓勵**締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]\n[36. **採納**本決議附件 III 所載之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍；]\n37. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為職權範圍中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；\n38. **強調**在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；\n39. **請求**執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：","html":"<p>30. <strong>注意到</strong>關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所需資金規模評估之報告；15<br />\n31. <strong>注意到</strong>符合資格之締約方提交之報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所需用於履行《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之資金規模，可用資訊有限；<br />\n[32. <strong>亦注意到</strong>針對全球環境基金第九期增資，對履行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需之必要且可用資金進行務實評估的重要性；]<br />\n[33. <strong>強調</strong>有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映於未來的評估中；]<br />\n[34. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 II 所載之職權範圍，旨在針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），根據締約方所提供之指引，針對協助開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下承諾所需之資金規模進行全面評估；並注意到該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]<br />\n[35. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]<br />\n[36. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 III 所載之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍；]<br />\n37. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為職權範圍中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；<br />\n38. <strong>強調</strong>在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；<br />\n39. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：</p>"},{"md":"[(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；]\n(b) 準備一份關於全面評估所需資金規模之報告，旨在根據締約方所提供之指引，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資，協助開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下承諾之情況，供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；\n[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是經全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織所認可之機構，以加速","html":"<p>[(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；]<br />\n(b) 準備一份關於全面評估所需資金規模之報告，旨在根據締約方所提供之指引，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資，協助開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下承諾之情況，供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；<br />\n[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是經全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織所認可之機構，以加速</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"15 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.","html":"<p>15 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.</p>"}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p008.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\nimplementation of the Framework, with an emphasis on improving access modalities[, including\ndirect access and [simplified][simplifying] procedures for developing country Parties], while\nensuring transparency, accountability, gender equality and the respect for human rights;]\n[(d) To report on the results of the collaboration and engagement mentioned in the\nsubparagraph above, and include options for such engagements, to the Subsidiary Body on\nImplementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]\n[(e) To facilitate the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities,\nwomen and youth in the implementation of the activities referred to in subparagraphs (a) to (d)\nabove.]\n\nAnnex I\nAdditional guidance to the Global Environment Facility\n[Placeholder for elements of guidance]\n\nAnnex II\nTerms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\nassist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and\nsmall island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\naccordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling\ntheir commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the\nGlobal Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034)\nA.\n\nObjective and scope\n\n1.\nThe objective of the work to be carried out under the present terms of reference is to enable\nthe Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity16 to make an assessment of\nthe amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least\ndeveloped countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\naccordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their\ncommitments under the Convention and its Protocols, in particular the commitment to implementing\nany successor to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 17 over the tenth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), and\ndetermine the amount of resources needed, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the\nConvention and decision III/8 of 15 November 1996 of the Conference of the Parties.\nB.\n\nMethodology\n\n2.\n\nThe funding needs assessment should be conducted taking into account:\n(a)\n\nArticle 20 and paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention, as well as the Framework;\n\n(b) Guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties, which\nmay call for future financial resources, and in the resource mobilization decision, in which the\nConference of the Parties calls for a broadening of the contributor base;\n(c) All obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and relevant decisions adopted\nby the Conference of the Parties, in particular the Framework;\n(d) National strategies, plans or programmes developed in accordance with Article 6 of the\nConvention and national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, where available;\n\n16 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n17 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n8/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"綱要之執行，重點在於改善取得模式[, 包括針對開發中締約方之直接取得與 [簡化][簡化] 程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權之尊重；]\n[(d) 就上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果進行報告，並向執行附屬機構提交此類參與之選項，該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議中提交；]\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 次段落所述活動之執行。]","html":"<p>綱要之執行，重點在於改善取得模式[, 包括針對開發中締約方之直接取得與 [簡化][簡化] 程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權之尊重；]<br />\n[(d) 就上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果進行報告，並向執行附屬機構提交此類參與之選項，該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議中提交；]<br />\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 次段落所述活動之執行。]</p>"},{"md":"附件 I\n給全球環境基金之額外指引\n[指引要素之預留位置]","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n給全球環境基金之額外指引<br />\n[指引要素之預留位置]</p>"},{"md":"附件 II\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約下之承諾，所需資金金額進行全面評估之任務說明書\nA.","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約下之承諾，所需資金金額進行全面評估之任務說明書<br />\nA.</p>"},{"md":"目標與範圍","html":"<p>目標與範圍</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使生物多樣性公約<sup>16</sup>締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定根據締約方大會所提供之指引，為協助開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約及其議定書下之承諾，特別是履行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>17</sup>之任何繼任者之承諾時，所需資金之金額，並根據公約第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使生物多樣性公約<sup>16</sup>締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定根據締約方大會所提供之指引，為協助開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約及其議定書下之承諾，特別是履行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>17</sup>之任何繼任者之承諾時，所需資金之金額，並根據公約第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。</p>"},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>"},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n資金需求評估應考量：\n(a) 公約第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及綱要；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n資金需求評估應考量：<br />\n(a) 公約第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及綱要；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引，該指引可能要求未來之財務資源，以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；\n(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是綱要；\n(d) 根據公約第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；","html":"<p>(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引，該指引可能要求未來之財務資源，以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；<br />\n(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是綱要；<br />\n(d) 根據公約第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；</p>"},{"md":"---\n<sup>16</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n<sup>17</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>16</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>17</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>"}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p009.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n(e) Information communicated to the Conference of the Parties in national reports and by\nthe Parties through the financial reporting framework and other submission responses to surveys and\ninterviews;\n(f)\nPolicies and guidelines agreed by the Council of the Global Environment Facility for\ndetermining eligibility for funding of projects;\n(g) Synergies with other biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral\nenvironmental agreements funded by the Global Environment Facility, including those with respect\nto operations and impacts;\n(h) Additional private capital mobilized through blended finance, including through the use\nof non-grant instruments, while recognizing the challenges that may be experienced by some Parties,\nin particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, in mobilizing private\ncapital in this regard;\n(i)\n\nPolicy coherence;\n\n(j)\nOther relevant estimations, including the costs of implementing the Gender Plan of\nAction (2023–2030);18\n[(k) Exchange rates, inflation volatility and the rising cost of conserving biodiversity in\ndeveloping economies.]\n3.\nIn the context of the assessment, interviews, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analyses, and\nconsultations should be undertaken, as needed for the preparation of the report, including:\n(a) A compilation and analysis of the needs identified in national biodiversity strategies and\naction plans and national biodiversity finance plans, including country-specific resource mobilization\nstrategies, prepared by Global Environment Facility-eligible and other relevant Parties pursuant to\nArticle 6 of the Convention, taking into account incremental cost funding as the fundamental\noperational principle of the Global Environment Facility;\n(b) A review of reports submitted by Parties pursuant to Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention,\nas well as Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety19 and Article 29 of the Nagoya Protocol\non Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their\nUtilization, 20 to identify funding needs related to the fulfilment of their obligations under the\nConvention and its Protocols;\n(c) The estimated financial implications of guidance provided to the financial mechanism\nby the Conference of the Parties;\n(d) A compilation and analysis of any supplementary information provided by Global\nEnvironment Facility-eligible Parties on their funding needs for the implementation of their\nobligations under the Convention and its Protocols.\nC.\n\nImplementation\n\n4.\nThe national focal points of the Convention and the focal points of the financial mechanism\n[should][may], as appropriate, bear joint responsibility for coordinating national-level incremental\nfunding needs assessments, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and other focal points under\nthe Convention and related conventions to ensure a whole-of-government approach.\n5.\nThe national focal points may establish a national platform or use existing national\ncoordination mechanisms, or both, to aid project planning, as necessary, and track ongoing\nbiodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities. Close links should be established between the\n\n18 Decision 15/11, annex.\n19 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n20 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619\n\n9/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會所通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構、以及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定專案資助資格之政策與指南；\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；\n(h) 透過混合金融（blended finance）所動員之額外私人資本，包括透過使用非撥款工具之方式，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本時可能面臨之挑戰；\n(i) 政策一致性；\n(j) 其他相關之估算，包括執行性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；$^{18}$\n[(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹波動，以及開發中經濟體在保育生物多樣性方面日益增加之成本。]","html":"<p>(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會所通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構、以及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；<br />\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定專案資助資格之政策與指南；<br />\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；<br />\n(h) 透過混合金融（blended finance）所動員之額外私人資本，包括透過使用非撥款工具之方式，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本時可能面臨之挑戰；<br />\n(i) 政策一致性；<br />\n(j) 其他相關之估算，包括執行性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；<sup>18</sup><br />\n[(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹波動，以及開發中經濟體在保育生物多樣性方面日益增加之成本。]</p>"},{"md":"3.\n在評估之脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮商，包括：\n(a) 彙編並分析在國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方根據《公約》第六條所編製之特定國家資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；\n(b) 審查締約方根據《公約》第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書$^{19}$》第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第二十九條所提交之報告$^{20}$，以識別與履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之義務相關之資助需求；\n(c) 估算締約方向財務機制提供之指引所產生的財務影響；\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之義務所需之資助需求，所提供之任何補充資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在評估之脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮商，包括：<br />\n(a) 彙編並分析在國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方根據《公約》第六條所編製之特定國家資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；<br />\n(b) 審查締約方根據《公約》第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<sup>19</sup>》第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第二十九條所提交之報告<sup>20</sup>，以識別與履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之義務相關之資助需求；<br />\n(c) 估算締約方向財務機制提供之指引所產生的財務影響；<br />\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之義務所需之資助需求，所提供之任何補充資訊。</p>"},{"md":"C. 執行","html":"<p>C. 執行</p>"},{"md":"4.\n《公約》之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點[應][可]視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資助需求評估，並與相關利害關係人以及《公約》及相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府（whole-of-government）之方法。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n《公約》之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點[應][可]視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資助需求評估，並與相關利害關係人以及《公約》及相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府（whole-of-government）之方法。</p>"},{"md":"5.\n國家聯絡點得視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資助需求、缺口與優先事項。應在","html":"<p>5.<br />\n國家聯絡點得視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資助需求、缺口與優先事項。應在</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{18}$ 決議 15/11，附件。\n$^{19}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{20}$ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>18</sup> 決議 15/11，附件。<br />\n<sup>19</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>20</sup> 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p010.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\nnational platform or relevant coordination mechanism and national support initiatives of relevant\nfunding providers, in particular the country engagement strategy of the Global Environment Facility.\n[6. The national platform should also facilitate the participation of indigenous peoples and local\ncommunities, women and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders, through a whole-ofsociety [and human rights-based] approach, as appropriate.]\n7.\nThe Executive Secretary should provide the information received from Parties without\nadditional reporting obligations on funding needs through an online platform, subject to the\navailability of resources, to facilitate the visualization of biodiversity funding needs, gaps and\npriorities on an ongoing basis.\n8.\nThe Executive Secretary should prepare a report on the full assessment, and the report should\nbe submitted for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before\nthe eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to providing recommendations\nfor consideration by the Conference of the Parties at that meeting.\n9.\nAt its eighteenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties will be invited to take note of the\nestimated amount of funds that are necessary for the implementation of the Convention and its\nProtocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund.\n\nAnnex III\nTerms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review\nof the effectiveness of the financial mechanism\nA.\n\nObjectives\n\n1.\nIn accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 21 of the Convention on Biological Diversity21 and\nbuilding upon the experience of the past six reviews of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism,\nthe Conference of the Parties to the Convention will undertake its seventh review at its eighteenth\nmeeting and take appropriate action to improve the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as\nnecessary. For that purpose, the following elements will be included in the review:\n(a) The conformity of the activities of the Global Environment Facility, as the institutional\nstructure operating the financial mechanism, with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties;\n(b) The effectiveness of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources to enable\n[all] eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\ndeveloping States, and Parties with economies in transition to meet the agreed full incremental costs\nto them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention\nand its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits, and benefit from their provisions,\ntaking into account the need for predictability, adequacy, accessibility and timely flow of funds,\nincluding the performance of the Global Environment Facility implementing agencies;\n(c) The efficiency of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources and, in\naccordance with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties, overseeing, monitoring and evaluating\nthe results of activities financed by its resources, including their social and gender- and equity-related\noutcomes and impacts, as relevant;\n(d) The effectiveness of catalysing and enhancing national implementation measures in line\nwith national priorities for achieving global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to\nthe Convention and its Protocols;\n(e) The efficiency and effectiveness of the activities funded by the Global Environment\nFacility and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the implementation of the Convention and\n\n21 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n\n10/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"國家平台或相關協調機制與相關出資者之國家支持倡議（特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略）之間建立密切聯繫。\n[6. 國家平台亦應透過全社會 [及以人權為基礎] 之適當方式，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。]","html":"<p>國家平台或相關協調機制與相關出資者之國家支持倡議（特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略）之間建立密切聯繫。<br />\n[6. 國家平台亦應透過全社會 [及以人權為基礎] 之適當方式，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。]</p>"},{"md":"7.\n**執行秘書**應在不增加額外報告義務之前提下，透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊（視資源可用性而定），以利持續視覺化生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>執行秘書</strong>應在不增加額外報告義務之前提下，透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊（視資源可用性而定），以利持續視覺化生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。</p>"},{"md":"8.\n**執行秘書**應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，以期為該次締約方大會之審議提供建議。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>執行秘書</strong>應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，以期為該次締約方大會之審議提供建議。</p>"},{"md":"9.\n在第十八次會議期間，將**邀請**締約方大會注意到全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，為履行《公約》及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n在第十八次會議期間，將<strong>邀請</strong>締約方大會注意到全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，為履行《公約》及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。</p>"},{"md":"附件 III\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍</p>"},{"md":"A.\n目標","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項²¹，並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，《公約》締約方將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提升財務機制之有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方指導原則之符合性；\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使[所有]符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之締約方，能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本，並從其規定中獲益；此處應考慮資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，並根據締約方之指導原則，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標），在催化與強化國家執行措施方面之有效性；\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於履行《公約》與","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項²¹，並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，《公約》締約方將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提升財務機制之有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：<br />\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方指導原則之符合性；<br />\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使[所有]符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之締約方，能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本，並從其規定中獲益；此處應考慮資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；<br />\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，並根據締約方之指導原則，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；<br />\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標），在催化與強化國家執行措施方面之有效性；<br />\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於履行《公約》與</p>"},{"md":"---\n²¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p>²¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p011.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\nthe achievement of its three objectives, as well as, as applicable, the implementation of its Protocols,\ntaking into account the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n(f)\nThe efficiency and effectiveness of processes and procedures for the deployment and\nuse of resources, including simplified procedures and access modalities;\n(g) The effectiveness and efficiency of the support provided for the objectives of the\nConvention and its Protocols in synergy with the implementation of other relevant multilateral\nenvironmental agreements, in a manner that is consistent with the mandates of the respective\nagreements;\n(h) The effectiveness in improving access to financial resources and trends associated with\nfunding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth to support the\nimplementation of the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols;\n(i)\nThe efficiency of each of the implementing agencies of the Global Environment Facility\nin providing technical support and services to countries in their preparation of project proposals and\nthe implementation of projects, including with regard to the timely disbursement of fund, fees and\nproject management costs, use of international consultants and control of expenditure.\nB.\n\nMethodology\n\n2.\nThe review will cover all the activities of the institutional structure operating the financial\nmechanism, in particular for the period from 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2026.\n3.\nThe review shall draw upon, inter alia, and in a balanced manner, the following sources of\ninformation:\n(a) The reviews of effectiveness of the financial mechanism in implementing the\nConvention undertaken pursuant to the memorandum of understanding between the Conference of\nthe Parties to the Convention and the Council of the Global Environment Facility, as contained in the\nannex to decision III/8 of 15 November 1996;\n(b) Reports prepared by the Global Environment Facility, including its reports for meetings\nof the Conference of the Parties to the Convention;\n(c) Reports of the Independent Evaluation Office of the Global Environment Facility that\nrelate to the biodiversity-related activities of the Facility, including the eighth comprehensive\nevaluation of the Global Environment Facility, as well as relevant assessments by the agencies\naccredited by the Council of the Facility and other partners;\n[(d) The Multilateral Performance Network assessments of the Global Environment Facility\nand reports related to the review of the vertical climate and environmental funds under the Group of\n20;22]\n(e) Information regarding the financial mechanism provided by Parties through national\nreports and other submissions, surveys and interviews;\n(f)\nInformation provided by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and\nrelevant stakeholders related to projects funded through the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\nand the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including their views on possible impacts on their\nrights, as applicable, as well as documented evidence and assessments of such impacts, including\ngender-differentiated impacts;\n(g)\n\nExperience with, and lessons learned from, relevant international financial mechanisms;\n\n(h) The report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth\nmeeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n\n22 See www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html.\n\n11/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"其三項目標之達成，以及（如適用）其議定書之履行，並考慮締約方大會所提供的指引；\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之履行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權保持一致之情況下，為公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的效能與效率；\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與支持原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以履行公約及其議定書目標相關之資金趨勢；\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國準備計畫提案及執行計畫時，提供技術支持與服務之效率，包括有關資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控制。","html":"<p>其三項目標之達成，以及（如適用）其議定書之履行，並考慮締約方大會所提供的指引；<br />\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；<br />\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之履行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權保持一致之情況下，為公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的效能與效率；<br />\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與支持原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以履行公約及其議定書目標相關之資金趨勢；<br />\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國準備計畫提案及執行計畫時，提供技術支持與服務之效率，包括有關資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控制。</p>"},{"md":"B. 方法論","html":"<p>B. 方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。</p>"},{"md":"3.\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，所進行之關於財務機制在履行公約方面之效能審查；\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；\n[(d) 多邊績效網絡對全球環境基金之評估，以及與二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告；]$^{22}$\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括（如適用）其對其權利可能造成影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；\n(g) 與相關國際財務機制之經驗及經驗教訓；\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；","html":"<p>3.<br />\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：<br />\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，所進行之關於財務機制在履行公約方面之效能審查；<br />\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；<br />\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；<br />\n[(d) 多邊績效網絡對全球環境基金之評估，以及與二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告；]<sup>22</sup><br />\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；<br />\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括（如適用）其對其權利可能造成影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；<br />\n(g) 與相關國際財務機制之經驗及經驗教訓；<br />\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{22}$ 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>22</sup> 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。</p>"}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p012.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n(i)\nThe stocktake review of the operations and performance of the Global Biodiversity\nFramework Fund regarding its scale, speed and accessibility and the future arrangements requested\nin decision 15/15 of 19 December 2022.\nC.\n\nCriteria\n\n[4.\nThe effectiveness and efficiency of the financial mechanism should be assessed taking\ninto account, inter alia:]\n(a) The actions taken by the Global Environment Facility in response to the guidance of the\nConference of the Parties and to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,23 including\nthrough the decisions of the Global Environment Facility Council on relations with conventions and\ninternational institutions;\n(b) The extent to which eligible Parties[, including developing countries, in particular the\nleast developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in\ntransition] take measures to apply for and receive timely, adequate and predictable funding to enable\nthem to meet the agreed full incremental cost to them of implementing measures through which they\nfulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental\nbenefits;\n[(c) Information provided by Parties in relation to their performance in delivering projects\nunder the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund,\nincluding on the effectiveness and efficiency of access modalities, constraints affecting women’s\naccess to financing, the competence and capacity of recipient Parties to maintain those modalities\nand the performance of implementing agencies;]\n[(d) Percentage of eligible Parties that have received financial support from the financial\nmechanism for implementing global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the\nConvention and its Protocols;]\n(e) Percentage of biodiversity-relevant funding through the financial mechanism in support\nof the achievement of global biodiversity goals and targets;\n(f)\nTrends in co-financing, in particular private and non-grant financing in the biodiversity\nfocal area enabled by the financial mechanism;\n(g) Trends in financing global, regional and subregional biodiversity projects under the\nfinancial mechanism;\n(h) Trends in financing that take into consideration synergies among conventions for which\nthe Global Environment Facility has been designated to operate their financial mechanism on an\nongoing and interim basis;\n(i)\nTrends in financing targeted at biodiversity-related conventions and agreements taking\ninto consideration synergies among them;\n[(j) Trends in time frames for project development and resource disbursement, including the\ntime between the approval of the concept note (or the project identification form) and the [first\ndisbursement][moment the recipient country received the resources];]\n[(k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities,\nwomen and youth and that respect, protect and fulfil human rights, including [direct] access to\nfinance;]\n[(l) Trends in the number and themes of capacity-building activities that enable Parties and\nstakeholders to secure access to financing from the Global Environment Facility;]\n\n23 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n12/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"(i)\n針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金在規模、速度與可近性方面之運作與績效進行檢視，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排。","html":"<p>(i)<br />\n針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金在規模、速度與可近性方面之運作與績效進行檢視，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排。</p>"},{"md":"C.","html":"<p>C.</p>"},{"md":"標準","html":"<p>標準</p>"},{"md":"[4.\n應考量下列事項（包括但不限於）來評估財務機制之有效性與效率：]\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》$^{23}$ 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；\n(b) 合格締約方[（包括開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方）]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本；\n[(c) 締約方就其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案之績效所提供之資訊，包括關於取得模式之有效性與效率、影響女性取得融資之限制、受援締約方維持該等模式之能力與職能，以及執行機構之績效；]\n[(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得資金支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；]\n(e) 透過財務機制用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；\n(g) 透過財務機制資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之資助趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責執行該等公約之財務機制；\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性資助趨勢；\n[(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括概念說明書（或專案識別表）獲核准至[首次撥款][受援國收到資源之時刻]之間的時間；]\n[(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年所領導，且尊重、保護並履行人權之資助趨勢，包括[直接]取得融資之管道；]\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人得以從全球環境基金獲得融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]","html":"<p>[4.<br />\n應考量下列事項（包括但不限於）來評估財務機制之有效性與效率：]<br />\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>23</sup> 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；<br />\n(b) 合格締約方[（包括開發中締約方，特別是最低開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方）]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本；<br />\n[(c) 締約方就其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案之績效所提供之資訊，包括關於取得模式之有效性與效率、影響女性取得融資之限制、受援締約方維持該等模式之能力與職能，以及執行機構之績效；]<br />\n[(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得資金支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；]<br />\n(e) 透過財務機制用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；<br />\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；<br />\n(g) 透過財務機制資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；<br />\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之資助趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責執行該等公約之財務機制；<br />\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性資助趨勢；<br />\n[(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括概念說明書（或專案識別表）獲核准至[首次撥款][受援國收到資源之時刻]之間的時間；]<br />\n[(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年所領導，且尊重、保護並履行人權之資助趨勢，包括[直接]取得融資之管道；]<br />\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人得以從全球環境基金獲得融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]</p>"},{"md":"$^{23}$ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>23</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>"},{"md":"12/13","html":"<p>12/13</p>"}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adba0140a679827eb07b236/p013.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 2 – 23 October 2026\n\n[(m) Trends in project financing leading to high sustainability or durability ratings and longterm results achieved through biodiversity programming supported by the Global Environment\nFacility in relation to expected results planned by the Facility through that programming;]\n[(n)\n\nCriteria listed in decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025.]\n\n[5. The assessment should include a comparison of the Global Environment Facility with the\nfinancial mechanisms of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including the Green\nClimate Fund[,][ and] the Adaptation Fund [and the Fund for Responding to Loss and Damage].\nElements for consideration should include: contributor base; funding modalities and financial\nperformance; criteria and processes for funding, including project cycle considerations; access and\ndisbursement modalities (e.g. direct allocation or project-based disbursement), including for\nindigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth; relationship between the governing\nbody of the fund and the Conference of the Parties to the respective multilateral environmental\nagreement; transparency, monitoring, reporting and evaluation; accreditation process and role and\nperformance of implementing agencies; cost-effectiveness of operations; ability to leverage funding\nto mobilize additional finance for biodiversity; cost of setting up and running the financial\ninstrument; leveraging public and private co-finance; and integration of various environmental\nfields.]\nD.\n\nProcedures for implementation\n\n[6. In consultation with the Bureau, the Executive Secretary will contract an experienced\nindependent evaluator to undertake the review, in accordance with the aforementioned objectives,\nmethodology and criteria.]\n[7. The evaluator will undertake desk studies, questionnaire surveys, interviews and field visits,\nsuch as may be required for the implementation of the review, and collaborate for that purpose with\nthe Global Environment Facility and its Independent Evaluation Office, as well as other independent\nassessments, such as those of the Multilateral Performance Network, if necessary, and prepare a\ncompilation and synthesis of the information received.]\n[8. Special efforts should be made to collect the views of Parties, the private sector, indigenous\npeoples and local communities, women and youth, including[, as applicable,] information on possible\nimpacts on their rights [in relation to project-specific environmental objectives and in accordance\nwith relevant national legislation].]\n[9. The draft synthesis report and recommendations of the evaluator will be made available to the\nGlobal Environment Facility for its review and comments. Such comments will be included in the\ndocumentation and identified by source.]\n[10. The report should include as an annex the study requested in paragraph 41 of decision 16/33\nof 27 February 2025 benchmarking the Global Environment Facility against the financial\nmechanisms or similar instruments of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements,\nincluding with regard to their legal nature, funding modalities and financial performance, criteria and\nprocess for funding, access and disbursement modalities, monitoring and evaluation, governance and\nthe cost-effectiveness of operations[, as well as other criteria contained in decision 16/34].]\n10 bis.\n\nThe report shall include as an annex the stocktake review referred to in decision 15/15.\n\n[11. On the basis of the synthesis report and recommendations of the independent evaluator, the\nExecutive Secretary will prepare, in consultation with the Global Environment Facility, a draft\ndecision on the seventh quadrennial review of the financial mechanism, including specific\nsuggestions for action to improve the effectiveness of the mechanism[, if necessary,] for\nconsideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, with its recommendations to be submitted\nto the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting.]\n__________\n13/13","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>"},{"md":"[(m) 專案融資趨勢所導致的高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所預期達成之成果之關係；]\n[(n)\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]","html":"<p>[(m) 專案融資趨勢所導致的高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所預期達成之成果之關係；]<br />\n[(n)<br />\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]</p>"},{"md":"[5. 評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及損失與損害回應基金]。應考慮之要素包括：出資者基礎；資助模式與財務績效；資助標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以動員額外生物多樣性資金之能力；建立與運行財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]","html":"<p>[5. 評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及損失與損害回應基金]。應考慮之要素包括：出資者基礎；資助模式與財務績效；資助標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以動員額外生物多樣性資金之能力；建立與運行財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]</p>"},{"md":"D. 執行程序","html":"<p>D. 執行程序</p>"},{"md":"[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]\n[7. 評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視審查執行之需求而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私營部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於其權利可能受影響之資訊 [與特定專案之環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]\n[9. 評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件並註明來源。]\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究，該研究將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]","html":"<p>[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]<br />\n[7. 評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視審查執行之需求而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]<br />\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私營部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於其權利可能受影響之資訊 [與特定專案之環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]<br />\n[9. 評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件並註明來源。]<br />\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究，該研究將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]</p>"},{"md":"10 bis.","html":"<p>10 bis.</p>"},{"md":"報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所提之清查審核。","html":"<p>報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所提之清查審核。</p>"},{"md":"[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議[, 如有必要,]，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。]\n__________\n13/13","html":"<p>[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議[, 如有必要,]，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>13/13</p>"}]}]};
